# Module-signing key pair (ECDSA P-256) — generate with:
#   python3 tools/gen_module_keys.py   (configure also does it on demand)
# The private key must never be committed; the public header is derived from it,
# so the pair is always regenerated together.  The kernel build regenerates the
# header into its own build directory on every ksym.c change.
Cact/crypto/modsign/

# Console font (PSF2, 8x8, 256 glyphs) — generate with:
#   python3 tools/gen_consolefont.py
# The kernel reads /usr/share/consolefont.psf from the image at boot, and the
# image build renders that copy from the same generator, so the font is never
# committed here.
tools/consolefont.psf
